// linear-search-x.lmc - look for a number in a row of 8 (extended LMC, NOT part of OCR's LMC)
// Input: a number to find.  Output: its position in the row, counting from 0, or 999 if it is not there.
// The row holds 12 7 33 5 21 8 19 4.   Input: 33  ->  Output: 2      Input: 50  ->  Output: 999
        INP
        STA target
        LDX #0          // start at the first place in the row
look    LDA data,X      // data[X]
        SUB target
        BRZ found       // 0 means data[X] equals the target
        INX
        TXA
        SUB #8          // looked at all 8?
        BRZ missing
        BRA look
found   TXA             // X is the position
        OUT
        HLT
missing LDA #999
        OUT
        HLT
target  DAT
data    DAT 12
        DAT 7
        DAT 33
        DAT 5
        DAT 21
        DAT 8
        DAT 19
        DAT 4
